@format 1
@id export.change-quality
@title Change encoding quality
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Build the video or audio quality control, synchronize supported bitrate entry, and show why ranged non-bitrate quality values cannot be typed manually.
@section I. UI
@tabs Split, Edit, Convert, Audio, Merge
@flow TB
@related export.apply-preset, export.commit-modifications
@tag quality
@tag encoder

@alias video = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSEncoder
@alias audio = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSEncoder
@alias field = Cadroue.UIShell.PSShared.PSField
@alias encoder = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSEncoder

[input] Encoder quality row requested <input>
- Resolve the selected video rate-control mode and its quality capability @ video.PSVideoQualityBuild(...)
- Resolve the selected audio rate-control mode and its quality capability @ audio.PSAudioQualityBuild(...)
> shape

[shape] Select quality-control shape <decision>
- Create a text box for the stored or default quality value @ field.PSEntryBuild(...)
? "Quality has no numeric range" > free-entry
? "Quality is a ranged bitrate" > bitrate
? "Quality is another ranged numeric value" > slider

[free-entry] Use editable text entry <process>
- Present the quality text box without a slider or read-only conversion @ video.PSVideoQualityBuild(...)
> apply

[bitrate] Synchronize slider and manual entry <process>
- Keep the bitrate text box editable and update the slider when valid text is entered @ field.PSFieldBitrateBuild(...)
- Update the text box when the bitrate slider moves @ field.PSFieldBitrateBuild(...)
> apply

[slider] Restrict input to slider <error>
- Mark the quality readout as read-only @ field.PSFieldSliderBuild(...)
- Replace its text only when the slider value changes @ field.PSFieldSliderBuild(...)
> apply

[apply] Store displayed quality <storage>
- Copy the displayed video and audio quality text into the edited preset when Apply or OK is pressed @ encoder.PSEncoderApply(...)
> result

[result] Quality value stored <output>
= Bitrate and unbounded quality fields accept typed input, while ranged non-bitrate quality fields can only be changed through the slider.
